### Medium-Severity Findings

#### 5. Eager Test
**Academic name:** Eager Test (Peruma et al. 2020)
**Affected:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (lines 57–63)

```csharp
// ❌ 7 distinct production methods called in one test
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);
```

**Fix:** Split into focused unit tests per method. If end-to-end coverage is desired, mark this as an integration test:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Integration")]
public void OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
```

**Risk if unfixed:** A failure could come from any of 7 methods — diagnosis is time-consuming.

