#### 9. Assertion Roulette
**Academic name:** Assertion Roulette (van Deursen et al. 2001; Peruma et al. 2020)
**Affected:** `CalculateTotal_ReturnsCorrectAmount` (lines 84–86)

```csharp
// ❌ 3 assertions, none with a message — which one failed?
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount);
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m, order.TaxAmount);
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal);
```

**Fix:** Add descriptive messages:

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(expectedSubtotal, order.TotalAmount, "Subtotal mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(expectedTax, order.TaxAmount, "Tax mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(expectedGrand, order.GrandTotal, "Grand total mismatch");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** A failure reports only `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<247.50> Actual:<0>` with no indication of which property was wrong.

